[test-suite name=math
  [doc [#
conformance fixtures for cx-stdlib/math (spec/std-lib/math.md §6).

   Each program imports the bundled module via [?lib 'cx-stdlib/math']
   (resolver MUST be quoted) then calls [$math:fn args]. The LAST
   expression is the rendered result. Sequence arguments use paren
   form (a, b, c). Error fixtures use out-err with the bare CXER code.

   Float grounding policy: the runner renders floats at full IEEE-754
   precision and compares token-by-token, while the spec quotes only
   approximate (≈) values. So irrational / transcendental results are
   asserted indirectly — via math/round-to to the spec's stated
   precision, via exact-identity compositions (e.g. log(e)=1,
   cos(0)=1), via predicates (is-finite / is-nan), or via the error
   cases — never by an invented full-precision literal. Exact integral
   results from §6 (pow(2,10)=1024, log10(100)=2, gcd(12,18)=6, …) are
   asserted directly.

   Error codes (§5): CXER3000 E_MATH_OVERFLOW, CXER3001
   E_MATH_EMPTY_SEQUENCE, CXER3002 E_MATH_DECIMAL_NOT_SUPPORTED,
   CXER3003 E_MATH_DOMAIN_ERROR.
#]]

 # ── §3.1 Basic ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 [case id=math-001-abs-negative-int level=core
  [tags math abs basic]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/math']
[$math:abs -5]
#]]
  [out-text [#
5
#]]
 ]

